  m_Name: Carta_CapturaDeCarbonoUrbana
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: Captura de Carbono Urbana
  _titleEn: Urban Carbon Capture
  _category: 0
  _unlockTrigger: 0
  _summary: "A captura direta do ar usa filtros e energia para tirar g\xE1s carb\xF4nico
    da atmosfera e guard\xE1-lo no subsolo."
  _summaryEn: Direct air capture uses filters and energy to pull carbon dioxide out
    of the atmosphere and store it underground.
  _realWorld: "A usina Orca, da Climeworks, ligada em 2021 na Isl\xE2ndia, captura
    at\xE9 cerca de 4 mil toneladas de CO2 por ano, uma fra\xE7\xE3o m\xEDnima das
    emiss\xF5es mundiais."
  _realWorldEn: Climeworks' Orca plant, switched on in Iceland in 2021, captures
    up to about 4,000 tonnes of CO2 a year, a tiny fraction of global emissions.
  _tradeOffs: "O custo por tonelada \xE9 muito alto, a tecnologia gasta muita energia,
    e ela n\xE3o substitui cortar as emiss\xF5es."
  _tradeOffsEn: The cost per tonne is very high, the technology uses a lot of energy,
    and it does not replace cutting emissions.
  _sources:
  - Label: Orca (Wikipedia)
    Url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orca_(carbon_capture_plant)
  - Label: Climeworks (Wikipedia)
    Url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Climeworks
